  "description": "Haridwar, meaning 'Gateway to God', is one of the seven holiest cities of India. Situated on the banks of the sacred River Ganga, the city is renowned for its spiritual atmosphere, ancient temples, holy ghats, yoga centers, and the mesmerizing Ganga Aarti at Har Ki Pauri. Millions of pilgrims and tourists visit Haridwar every year to experience its faith, culture, and natural beauty.",

